 "quotes": [
  {
   "id": "Q01",
   "text": "Ask Claude for a deck, and you get a deck."
  },
  {
   "id": "Q02",
   "text": "Replace the noun with verbs."
  },
  {
   "id": "Q03",
   "text": "A quarterly review isn't a deck. It's getting busy people to believe a story about cause and effect and to decide under uncertainty in 30 minutes."
  },
  {
   "id": "Q04",
   "text": "Then a red team to attack it, a short seller, and a forensic accountant."
  },
  {
   "id": "Q05",
   "text": "And have Claude do what a short seller does to research a position, not write like one."
  },
  {
   "id": "Q06",
   "text": "Role-play makes the transcript weirder, not the result better."
  },
  {
   "id": "Q07",
   "text": "Now that multi-agent setups are easier to run, he's seen really interesting results asking Claude to bring in extra fields."
  },
  {
   "id": "Q08",
   "text": "Nouns to verbs, then the crew",
